<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       id="ticket" title="/ticket ✏️">

    <tldr>
        <p>
            <format style="italic">Manage ticket channels and interactions.</format>
        </p>

        <p><br/></p>

        <p>
            <format style="bold">Allowed in DMs:</format>
            :x: No
        </p>

        <p>
            <format style="bold">Default permission required:</format>
            <code>None</code> (context-dependent)
        </p>
    </tldr>

    <chapter title="Description" id="description">
        <p>
            The <code>/ticket</code> command provides subcommands for managing ticket channels.
            These commands allow support staff and ticket creators to close tickets, add users, and perform other ticket-related actions.
            All ticket commands must be used within a ticket channel and are subject to permission checks based on the ticket panel configuration.
        </p>
        <p>
            For a complete overview of the ticket system, see <a href="Ticket-System.md">Ticket System</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Sub-Commands" id="sub-commands">
        <list>
            <li><a href="ticket-close.topic">/ticket close</a>: Close the current ticket channel (if the panel isn't <code>closeable</code>, the ticket will be deleted instead).</li>
            <li><a href="ticket-add.topic">/ticket add</a>: Add a user to the current ticket channel (support staff only).</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            Additional ticket actions (claim, unclaim, delete, reopen, transcript) are available via button interactions within ticket channels, but might be added as sub-commands at a later date.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="See Also" id="see-also">
        <list>
            <li><a href="Ticket-System.md">Ticket System Overview</a></li>
            <li><a href="Ticket-Panel-Configuration.md"/></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

</topic>
